<title>CHINA: Fannie Mae sets HK$1.5 bln global bond.</title>
<headline>Fannie Mae sets HK$1.5 bln global bond.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following issue was announced by lead manager HSBC Markets.</p>
<p> BORROWER FANNIE MAE</p>
<p> AMT	HK$1.5 BLN    COUPON     6.85 PCT MATURITY 29.JUL.02</p>
<p> TYPE     GLOBAL BOND   ISS PRICE  99.832   PAY DATE 29.JUL.97</p>
<p> LAST MOODY AAA	   REOFFER    99.832   LAUNCHED 09.JUL.97</p>
<p> LAST S&amp;P   AAA	   SPREAD     *	  DENOM    HK$500K</p>
<p> LISTING    HK &amp; LUXEMBOURG		     PAY FREQ ANNUALLY</p>
<p> SALE LMTS  US/UK/HK</p>
<p> FULL FEES 25 BP	  MGT/UND    10 BP    SELL CONC 15 BP</p>
<p> GOV LAW   NEW YORK     HOME CTRY  U.S.</p>
<p> LEAD MANAGERS HSBC MARKETS AND MERRILL LYNCH INTERNATIONAL</p>
<p>NOTES  *SPREAD IS 34.5 BASIS POINTS OVER THE JUNE 2002 6.55</p>
<p>	  PERCENT HK EXCHANGE FUND NOTES AND 61.6 BASIS POINTS</p>
<p>	  OVER THE JUNE 2002 6.25% US TREASURY.</p>
<p>**CLEARING THROUGH CENTRAL MONEYMARKETS UNIT/ EUROCLEAR/CEDEL</p>
<p>***THE ISSUE IS THE FIRST HONG KONG DOLLAR GLOBAL BOND</p>
<p>--Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2847 4039</p>
</text>
